From 9f4c7c374fbaf68236d05c983ec60069488dc3a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vincenzo Grimaldi <vince.ceccarelli@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 18:51:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0034 a funding print is a print, not a tick (5501 passed)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

INVENTORY D1: main.tick calls on_candle every 60 s with the ticker's
PREDICTED rate, and the engine booked it on every call. 60 ticks at 1 bps on
$100 booked $0.60; one real 8h print is $0.01. The negative-funding streak
and the 8-print EWMA counted ticks too: three negative MINUTES unwound the
book, and the EWMA was eight minutes of one number.

Fix — prints carry their settlement stamp:

  CarryBroker.get_funding_print(symbol) -> (bps, settlement_ms), from
    /v5/market/funding/history (the settled record), not the ticker (F6).
    Raises when unreadable.
  take_snapshot reads it directly (no getattr) and keeps the forecast
    (funding_bps) and the settled print (funding_print_bps/_ms) apart.
  assert_fresh refuses a settled print older than one funding interval
    (Bybit instrument fundingInterval = 480 min — a venue fact, not a tuned
    threshold) plus the existing snapshot age limit: a missed settlement is a
    stale view. A print stamped in the future is refused too.
  CarryEngine.on_candle(..., funding_print_ms): only a stamp newer than the
    last is a print. It enters the EWMA once, counts toward the streak once,
    and is booked once — and only if the pair was held through it (stamp
    after the open). No stamp, no print: nothing booked, the warm-up cannot
    complete, the book cannot open.
  D10: every held print is booked SIGNED; negative prints were paid and
    never booked.
  main.tick passes the settled print and its stamp; logs settled AND
    predicted.

The settlement-clock backtest (0032) already counts prints this way, so
engine and simulation now agree on what "three negative prints" means —
which is the rule that produced D14's churn. Not retuned.

Tests first: tests/test_carry_funding_prints.py, 20 new (60 ticks of one
print book it once; entry print not collected; pre-open print not booked;
negative booked; 3 negative ticks hold, 3 negative prints unwind; EWMA sees
one observation per stamp; no stamp -> no entry; broker reads funding
history and raises on 4 malformed shapes; snapshot keeps both rates; missed
settlement and future stamp are stale; the tick passes the settled rate;
60 ticks through main.tick book one print).

TESTS CHANGED — fixtures only, no assertion edited: fake brokers in
test_market_snapshot / test_carry_live_gates / test_carry_wiring gain
get_funding_print; warm-up calls pass settlement stamps; test_carry_engine's
wired fixture stamps one print per candle (what those tests always meant by
"a print"); my own 0033 file stamps its candles.

